Add the flagship `smith` super-skill: a thin orchestrator that COMPOSES the
existing stage skills (triage-ready → claim-safety → plan → dev → validate →
ship → review → verify) into the right path for a piece of work, driving
autonomously between human gates and pausing at them. It invents no stage
logic — it picks the path by change classification, enforces the three human
gates as durable kernel events (forge gate check|approve|reject|status over
gate.intent · gate.plan-approval · gate.merge, so a gated run is resume-safe),
proves lease ownership via claim-safety/forge issue owns, and certifies
forge release check before close.

During planning, smith calibrates human-loop density from the issue's
size × importance × complexity, proposing an autonomy tier (lean/standard/high)
at the intent gate; the human confirms or overrides, and low confidence fails
toward more oversight. A Fork points section documents the heuristic, the
tier → gate-set mapping, gate density, and the composed flow.

Registered in the kernel umbrella skill and mirrored into .codex/skills via
skills-sync (generated, not hand-edited); added to the skills-structure
expected set. Skill doc only — no new stage code.

Closes 7da81cbd-f890-49dc-b237-9ce4729ed6be

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
